<title>USA: Hicks Muse, Capstar add 20 radio stations.</title>
<headline>Hicks Muse, Capstar add 20 radio stations.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN, Texas 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Capstar Broadcasting Partners said on Tuesday it and Hicks, Muse, Tate &amp; Furst Inc signed definitive agreements to buy 20 radio stations in mid-sized markets in a deal valued at $60 million.</p>
<p>Capstar was formed in May 1996 by principals of Hicks Muse, a private Dallas investment firm. Since then the two firms have bought or agreed to buy 120 mid-sized stations.</p>
<p>The current deal involves the purchase of radio groups in Alaska, Arizona, Virginia and Wisconsin.</p>
